                <pb facs="0835" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363 Manchuria/65: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-10-24T16:00:00+08:00">October 24, 1934—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 24—2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>485. Legation’s 484, October 24, 1 p.m. Chase reports that the Monopoly Bureau
                    has requested Chinese agents of the Standard-Vacuum Company to send delegates to
                    a meeting to be held at Hsinking on the 26th for the purpose of selecting
                    distributors of monopoly kerosene; that company have suggested to agents that
                    the Bureau be informed that the matter should be taken up directly with the
                    company.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
